# TASK-260715-vtot05 rework 04 contract

Remediate both material findings in the independent re-review 04 `TASK-260715-vtot05_results.md`. Preserve all previously verified AC1-AC4 and AC5 regressions.

## Language-specific lexical fixes

- Split comment/literal handling by language. C/C++/Objective-C and Go block comments are non-nesting: the first `*/` returns to code. Preserve Swift's language-appropriate comment/raw-string behavior separately.
- Normalize C/C++ alternative preprocessing tokens, including `%:%:` as token paste, before reconstructing forbidden symbol references.
- Tokenize Swift escaped identifiers (backticks) as identifiers, not Go raw strings.
- Parse Swift raw-string interpolation (`#"...\#(...)..."#` and supported pound counts) and inspect interpolation code for forbidden surfaces.
- Reject typed/inferred ambiguous Swift `.init(contentsOf:)` references unless the argument is structurally the approved explicit `URL(fileURLWithPath:)` local form. Preserve safe local `Data`/`String` controls.
- Add compiler-backed regressions for all six reviewer fixtures: C non-nesting-comment `system`, C `%:%:` token paste, Swift inferred `Data .init(contentsOf:)`, Swift raw interpolation `Process`, Swift escaped `Process`, and Go non-nesting-comment aliased `net/http`.
- Add adjacent safe/comment/raw-string controls so the lexer does not turn documentation-only text into false positives.

## CI history fix

- Ensure the exact workflow job running `relay-supply-chain-audit` checks out enough Git history to resolve both pinned provenance commits (`fetch-depth: 0` is acceptable).
- Add a static/workflow regression proving the history requirement is declared, and reproduce the audit from a fresh checkout shape representative of CI without any network fetch during the task.

Run the full adversarial suite, audit, manifest/linkage tests, Go tests/vet, unsigned Swift build, Actionlint/format/privacy/diff checks, deterministic double generation, and board validation. Do not weaken validation.

No signing, credentials/Keychain access, provider/app launch, VPN/network mutation, or physical validation.
# TASK-260715-vtot05 developer rework 04 results

Date: 2026-08-19
Role: developer / implementer
State: ready for independent review

## Implemented remediation

- Split runtime lexical handling by language. C/C++/Objective-C and Go block comments now terminate at the first `*/`; Swift retains nested block-comment behavior.
- Normalized C-family `%:%:` to the same token-paste surface as `##` before forbidden process/libcurl symbol reconstruction.
- Added Swift-specific parsing for escaped identifiers, nested comments, normal and pound-delimited raw strings, and code inside string interpolation.
- Made inferred or otherwise ambiguous Swift `.init(contentsOf:)` fail closed unless its argument is structurally the approved explicit `URL(fileURLWithPath:)` local form.
- Added compiler/preprocessor/typechecker-backed regressions for the six independent re-review 04 fixtures: C non-nesting comment `system`, C `%:%:` token paste, Swift inferred `Data .init(contentsOf:)`, Swift raw interpolation `Process`, Swift escaped `Process`, and Go non-nesting comment `net/http` import. Adjacent safe nested-comment, literal raw-string, raw-interpolation, escaped-identifier, Go raw-string, C comment, and explicit local-file controls remain accepted.
- Added `fetch-depth: 0` to the exact `relay-toolchain` CI checkout that runs the audit, plus a static test binding full history and `make relay-supply-chain-audit` to that job.
- Updated the bounded runtime-policy documentation and task logbook entry. AC1-AC4 provenance, notice, manifest linkage, privacy, and M2/M5 ownership data were preserved byte-for-byte by deterministic regeneration.

## Acceptance evidence

- AC1: The existing authoritative source/build/compiler/standard-library revision, content-hash, SPDX, notice, and provenance mapping remains audit-clean.
- AC2: Product notices and missing-approved-metadata coverage remain audit-clean; the generated notice hash is unchanged.
- AC3: Inventory/provenance/manifest/Swift linkage remains deterministic and privacy-clean; no credentials, workstation paths, private keys, or mutable URLs were introduced.
- AC4: The documented boundary still assigns M2 pinning/reproducibility/hashes/notices and concrete M5 signing/notarization/attestation/distribution tasks.
- AC5: The complete current runtime source surface remains fail-closed, all prior adversarial cases still reject, all six new compiler-valid bypasses now reject for the intended reason, safe local controls pass, and a full-history clean clone contains both pinned provenance commits and passes the audit without a network fetch.

